## What

Implement the **Sponsor-validated** S/MIME tier as a Profile type in `pkix-profiles-cabf`. Per CA/B Forum S/MIME BR §7.6.x: this tier has an employer or sponsoring organization vouching for the named individual. Includes both organization fields AND individual identity fields, plus the BR's "sponsor" semantics.

## API shape

```rust
/// Sponsor-validated S/MIME BR subscriber-certificate profile.
///
/// Reference, not authoritative. CA/B Forum S/MIME Baseline Requirements
/// v1.0.14 (or whichever revision the cabf workspace has refreshed to).
///
/// Asserts policy OID `2.23.140.1.5.3.1` (Sponsor-validated).
///
/// Required Subject DN fields per BR: organizationName, givenName + surname
/// (or pseudonym), serialNumber (subject-unique identifier per BR conventions).
/// Subject SAN: rfc822Name (one or more).
pub struct SmimeSponsorValidated;

impl Profile for SmimeSponsorValidated {
    fn policy(&self, now_unix: u64) -> ValidationPolicy {
        // - required_leaf_eku: id-kp-emailProtection
        // - require_rfc822_san: true
        // - max_validity: per BR §6.3.2
        // - required_policy_oids: [2.23.140.1.5.3.1]
        // - required_subject_dn_attributes: [organizationName, givenName + surname]
    }
    fn version(&self) -> &'static str { "1.0.14" }
}

pub const fn smime_sponsor_policy(now_unix: u64) -> ValidationPolicy {
    SmimeSponsorValidated.policy(now_unix)
}
```

## Test fixtures

Same dual-oracle convention as PKIX-jbvb.1 (zlint + pkilint cross-validation per Mark's 2026-05-11 decision option d). Positive: Sponsor-validated certs accepted by both oracles. Negative: certs from other tiers.

## Acceptance

- [ ] `pkix_profiles_cabf::SmimeSponsorValidated` ships and impls `Profile`
- [ ] `smime_sponsor_policy(now_unix)` free function alias exists
- [ ] Reference-not-authoritative rustdoc disclaimer
- [ ] Rustdoc cites CA/B Forum S/MIME BR v1.0.14 with correct section numbers (post-PKIX-d5rh refresh)
- [ ] At least 2 positive + 2 negative fixtures with provenance recorded
- [ ] Tests pass against both zlint + pkilint sourced fixtures
- [ ] CHANGELOG entry in `pkix-profiles-cabf`

## Out of scope

- Other tiers (PKIX-jbvb.1 Organization, PKIX-jbvb.3 Individual)
- "Auto-detect tier from cert policy OID" wrapper — caller-side concern

